Description: Sparky Stereo OS: one stereo output, the quad buffer, handed to Stereo KWin
 PyMOL keeps every way of reading molecules; its stereo OUTPUT is one: a quad
 buffer window (GLX_STEREO) that Mesa packs as full side by side and Stereo KWin
 shows on every screen.  The cross-eye, wall-eye, side-by-side, stencil,
 anaglyph, geowall, dynamic and OpenVR modes and the eye swap are not offered:
 "stereo MODE" and the menu entries are gone and stereo_mode is always the quad
 buffer.  The 3D options are "Enable 3D" (read when the window is made, because
 a window gets its quad buffer when it is created) and a shortcut to Display
 Settings.  Enable 3D is on unless the person turned it off: a screen with no
 quad buffer visual (a 2D desktop) stays 2D and PyMOL says nothing; when the
 person turned 3D on and the window has none, it says so in their language
 (ten languages, pymol/edition3d.py, also the sentences of the refused stereo
 commands) and stays 2D.  -S no longer forces a flat picture to pass for 3D
 (check_gl_stereo_capable).  PyMOL's own stereo_angle and stereo_shift
 camera settings are untouched.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
